==Goal-line technology==
The 2012 FIFA Club World Cup was the first FIFA tournament to use [[goal-line technology]] following its approval by the [[International Football Association Board]] (IFAB) in July 2012.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.supersport.com/football/article.aspx?Id=1464991|title=Goal-line tech to debut at Club World Cup|publisher=supersport.com|date=5 July 2012}}</ref> The two systems approved by FIFA, [[GoalRef]] (installed in Yokohama) and [[Hawk-Eye]] (installed in Toyota), were used in the two stadiums.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1954433/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130122114749/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1954433/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=22 January 2013|title=FIFA Club World Cup: GLT project agreements signed|publisher=FIFA|date=27 November 2012}}</ref>

==Matches==
The draw for the 2012 FIFA Club World Cup was held at the FIFA headquarters in [[Zürich]], [[Switzerland]], on 24 September 2012 at 11:30 [[Central European Summer Time|CEST]] ([[UTC+02:00]]).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1705222/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120925235828/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1705222/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=25 September 2012|title=Follow the draw LIVE on FIFA.com|publisher=FIFA|date=23 September 2012}}</ref> The draw decided the "positions" in the bracket for the three representatives which entered the quarter-finals (AFC/CAF/CONCACAF).<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1707178/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120926233032/http://www.fifa.com/clubworldcup/news/newsid=1707178/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=26 September 2012|title=Intriguing quarter-final pairings drawn|publisher=FIFA|date=24 September 2012}}</ref>

If a match was tied after normal playing time:<ref name="regulations">{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/01/95/45/34/regulationsfcwc2012_e.pdf|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20130328220018/http://www.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/01/95/45/34/regulationsfcwc2012%5fe.pdf|url-status=dead|archive-date=28 March 2013|title=Regulations – FIFA Club World Cup Japan 2012|publisher=FIFA}}</ref>
*For elimination matches, [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] was played. If still tied after extra time, a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]] was held to determine the winner.
*For the matches for fifth place and third place, no extra time was played, and a penalty shoot-out was held to determine the winner.

